## Optimize MCP server answer latency (6-phase perf pass) — backport

Context: MCP tool answers were slow. Tracing the path (MCP proxy → external
REST → DigitalTwin.resolve_domain → SQL triple store) showed the dominant cost
was per-request work paid on *every* read-only tool call: reloading the
PUBLISHED domain from the registry (newest→oldest version scan), regenerating
OWL/R2RML, and persisting the session. Secondary costs: an O(domains ×
versions) scan behind `list_domains`, a version N+1 for `/domain/versions`,
repeated full-table stats scans, a broken/wasted ontology-label POST in
`select_domain`, a fresh httpx client per tool call, and stacked cold-start
retries. Backported from the develop branch (cherry-pick of the perf pass);
`dt_stats` uses this line's `graph_name`/`get_triplestore` conventions.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/registry_cache.py
   Add a TTL-cached PUBLISHED-domain store (get/set_cached_published_domain)
   and invalidate it (namespaced `<cache_key>::<folder>`) with the other
   registry caches.
2. src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py
   Add `load_published_domain_data_cached` and rewrite `list_mcp_domains` to
   use the cached two-query metadata listing (filter by per-version PUBLISHED
   status) instead of scanning every version document.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   `resolve_domain(..., read_only=False)`: read_only paths serve the cached
   PUBLISHED doc, skip `ensure_generated_content()` and `save()`, plus phase
   timing log line.
4. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py
   `dt_status`/`dt_stats`/`dt_triples_find` resolve with `read_only=True`.
   `dt_stats`: 60s in-process result cache keyed by graph name + `run_blocking`
   + timing. `dt_triples_find`: BFS/alias/fetch moved off the event loop via
   `run_blocking` + timing.
5. src/api/routers/domains.py
   `/domain/versions` reads lifecycle status via the cheap `get_version_status`
   single-column lookup instead of loading each full version document.
6. src/mcp-server/server/app.py
   Shared pooled httpx AsyncClient (keep-alive reuse) via a non-closing async
   context manager; per-request GET/POST elapsed-ms logging; retry backoff
   trimmed to (2,5,10) and disabled for localhost/mounted mode; removed the
   broken ontology-label POST from `select_domain`; lowered `describe_entity`
   default limit 500 → 100.
7. tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py
   In-memory store returns realistic version metadata + `get_version_status`.
8. tests/units/registry/test_registry_published.py
   Cover cached published resolution and metadata-based `list_mcp_domains`.
9. tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py
   Cover `resolve_domain` read_only (cache + skip gen/save) vs write path.
10. tests/units/api/test_external_api.py
    Update `/domain/versions` test to mock `get_version_status`.

